# Generated from: specs/15-present-commitments-in-local-time-with-complete-context/requirements.md
Feature: Present commitments in local time with complete context
  As a volunteer
  I want every commitment shown in the group's local time with its duration, place, and instructions
  So that I can decide and arrive without converting UTC or finding a separate message

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Coordinator configures the group time zone
    Given no group time zone has been configured
    And an allowlisted coordinator is authenticated
    When the coordinator selects a valid IANA time zone
    Then the singleton setting is stored with optimistic concurrency
    And GroupTimeZoneConfigured identifies that coordinator in the audit trail
    And schedule forms use local date and time controls
    And persisted shift instants remain UTC

  @SCN002
  Scenario Outline: Daylight-saving exceptions require explicit correction
    Given the group time zone is America/New_York
    And the coordinator enters <local_time> for a shift boundary
    When the coordinator submits the schedule form without an offset choice
    Then the application <outcome>
    And no shift mutation occurs until one valid interpretation is supplied

    Examples:
      | local_time       | outcome                                                                    |
      | 2026-03-08 02:30 | explains that the time does not exist and requires another wall time       |
      | 2026-11-01 01:30 | displays both labelled UTC-offset interpretations and requires one choice  |

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Volunteer sees complete commitment context
    Given a published shift has a location, volunteer instructions, and a primary slot
    And the group time zone is configured
    When a volunteer browses, requests, checks status, and inspects an assignment action
    Then every surface labels the local start, local end, duration, zone and UTC offset, location, slot role, and instructions
    And semantic time values retain the authoritative UTC instants
    And internal coordinator notes never appear

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Unconfigured time zone reveals no private-link validity
    Given the group time zone is not configured
    And valid and invalid request-status and assignment-action tokens are presented
    When their GET and POST routes are requested
    Then every route shows the same textual commitment-times-unavailable state
    And no request, assignment, action token, notification, or audit state changes
    And no UTC fallback or token-validity detail appears

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Confirmed zone correction changes display not commitments
    Given future commitments exist as authoritative UTC instants
    And an allowlisted coordinator views the time-zone consequence warning
    When the coordinator confirms a change to another valid IANA zone
    Then GroupTimeZoneChanged records the actor and old and new zone identifiers
    And every stored shift instant is unchanged
    And every commitment surface immediately renders those instants in the new group zone

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Local commitment text remains accessible and deterministic
    Given a commitment crosses a local date or daylight-saving boundary
    When it is rendered in a browser with a different locale at a narrow mobile width
    Then start and end dates are explicit
    And elapsed duration is calculated from UTC instants
    And all state and context remain available as text without color or icons
